  "result": "I changed `archiveIssuesForProject` in `src/server/repositories/issue-repository.ts` so the project-archive cascade only touches issues that are still live.\n\nThe bug was in its `WHERE` clause, which matched every issue in the project. Issues archived weeks earlier were re-stamped with today's `archived_at`, and the returned count included them. That count feeds the `project.archived` event, so the usage service subtracted too much from the issues-used meter, which explains the drift and the negative reading.\n\nThe fix adds the shared `livePredicate(issues.archivedAt, {})` helper, the same one the other issue queries use, so already-archived rows are left alone and the returned count now reflects only the issues actually archived. Issues in other projects are still excluded by the existing `orgId` and `projectId` predicates.\n\nI haven't run the test suite; the dependency install and test run were outside what I could check in this session.",
